{"newRange":[8,25],"summary":"label and endquote record each label a quote names and refuse any without a matching resolution of at least 8 words.","rationale":"A quote such as 'lets go with B' means nothing to a reader who never saw the options, so the author words stay unchanged and a bracketed resolution carries the meaning. Labels are collected per quote block and resolved at block end. Verified by scripts/author-prompts-check under gawk and mawk; not run under macOS awk.","author":"fm/verilex-author-prompts-labels"},
{"newRange":[31,44],"summary":"Each quote line has its resolutions stripped, then the six label shapes are scanned on the lowercased remainder.","rationale":"Resolutions are removed first because their own text contains 'option B', which would otherwise count as an unresolved label. Word boundaries are written as character classes because awk has no \\b. The bare '> 1. a ...' shape also matches an article 'a', as the spec requires.","author":"fm/verilex-author-prompts-labels"}]},
{"path":"scripts/ci","summary":"Wires the new test as the author-prompts step and lints its script.","annotations":[{"newRange":[123,123],"summary":"The author-prompts step runs scripts/author-prompts-check.","rationale":"CI jobs test and test-macos call it through scripts/ci, so one entry point owns the test.","author":"fm/verilex-author-prompts-labels"}]}
